*.pyc

# Build output.
#
# The release zips are deliberately NOT versioned. They are build artifacts:
# `python build.py` reproduces any of them byte-for-byte from the matching
# tag, so committing them would store ~8 MB (and growing, one per release)
# of derivable data. On GitHub the right home for a release binary is the
# Releases tab, attached to its version tag.
#
# This does NOT contradict the house rule of keeping every old zip -- they
# stay on disk locally, untouched. Ignoring is not deleting.
#
# It also keeps the CI green: the last workflow step runs `python3 build.py`,
# and build.py REFUSES to overwrite an existing zip (on purpose, so a
# forgotten version bump fails loudly). With the current version's zip
# committed, a clean checkout would hit that refusal and go red on the very
# first push.
magpie_swatches-*.zip
dist/

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Art working files.
#
# The LOGO/ folder holds the Photoshop sources the shipped artwork was made
# from -- 2.5 MB of PSD and full-resolution PNG that nobody cloning this
# repository needs. They stay on disk locally, they just are not versioned.
#
# The whole folder, SVG included: the hook's shape follows a community
# standard rather than being an original design, so there is no originality
# claim for a source file to evidence. hook_shape.py carries the outline as
# plain coordinates and cites the pattern's origin in its own docstring.
LOGO/

# Internal decision records.
#
# The docs/decisions/*.md files record why each calibrated number is the
# value it is, and they stay on the author's machine only -- they are
# working notes in Portuguese, not documentation for anyone cloning this.
# README.md and CHANGELOG.md carry everything an outside reader needs.
docs/
